            <ArticleTitle>Factors influencing occupational back pain in Bedfordshire.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>254-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper reports on a pilot study of occupational back pain among a sample of 68 men aged 16 to 65 years in the North Bedfordshire Health District, England. In a multidisciplinary appraoch, measurements of 126 variables for each case were made. It was found that driving high mileages was a significant factor affecting both occurrence and location of pain. Certain personality factors were also significant.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
